Node.js is built as a shared library (libnode) that can be embedded in C++ applications.

CMake Integration:

    find_package(node CONFIG REQUIRED)
    target_link_libraries(my_app PRIVATE node::libnode)

To embed Node.js in your C++ application:

    #include <node.h>
    #include <uv.h>
    #include <v8.h>

See the Node.js Embedder API documentation:
    https://nodejs.org/api/embedding.html

The following headers are available:
    - node.h, node_version.h - Node.js core API
    - node_api.h, node_api_types.h - Node.js N-API
    - node_buffer.h, node_object_wrap.h - Additional APIs
    - v8/*.h - V8 JavaScript engine headers
    - uv.h - libuv event loop headers

Example C++ embedding code is provided in the examples directory.
